  { q: 'Which Siberian peoples use the raven in shamanism?', a: 'The raven features in the shamanic traditions of multiple Siberian and Northeast Asian peoples: the Chukchi, Koryak, and Itelmen (Kamchatka Peninsula) have the raven as a major creator figure; the Evenki, Yukagir, and other taiga peoples include the raven among shamanic helper spirits; the Yakut (Sakha) have raven-associated clan totems and shamanic narratives. There is also significant cultural overlap with Yupik and Inuit traditions across the Bering Strait, where parallel raven creator myths appear — suggesting ancient circumpolar transmission of raven mythology.' },
